<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">24 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 24 January, from 41 to 1984.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/caligula" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/caligula.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">41 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,985 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Emperor Caligula assassinated by his guards</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Praetorian officers led by Cassius Chaerea stabbed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caligula">Caligula</a> in a palace corridor during the Palatine games. The Guard then made his uncle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudius">Claudius</a> emperor.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">771 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,255 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">K'ak' Tiliw Chan Yopaat dedicates Stela E at Quiriguá</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kak-tiliw-chan-yopaat">K'ak' Tiliw Chan Yopaat</a>, ruler of the Maya city of Quiriguá, dedicated Stela E in its Great Plaza. Carved with his portraits and weighing some 65 tons, it was the largest stone ever quarried by the ancient Maya.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kak-tiliw-chan-yopaat">K'ak' Tiliw Chan Yopaat</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">914 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,112 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Fatimids launch their first invasion of Egypt</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Fatimid army under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> general Habasa ibn Yusuf left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripoli">Tripoli</a> to attack Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, taking the coastal route through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrenaica">Cyrenaica</a>. The invasion took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a> but failed before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fustat">Fustat</a>, and the remnants returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifriqiya">Ifriqiya</a> in May 915.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1438">1438 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">588 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Council of Basel suspends Pope Eugene IV</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The members of the council who had stayed at Basel after Eugene IV moved it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferrara">Ferrara</a> affirmed its ecumenical character and suspended the pope. They later declared him deposed and elected the antipope Felix V, a former Duke of Savoy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-basel">Council of Basel</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-eugene-iv">Pope Eugene IV</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1848">1848 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">178 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gold found at Sutter's Mill sparks the California Gold Rush</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">James Marshall spotted flakes of gold in the tailrace of a sawmill at Coloma. Within a few years some 300,000 people had flooded into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a>, which became a state in 1850.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1908">1908 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">118 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Baden-Powell publishes 'Scouting for Boys'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The first instalment of Robert Baden-Powell's handbook on outdoor skills and citizenship appeared in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>. Boys began forming patrols of their own, and the Scout movement spread worldwide.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1915">1915 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">111 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">British battlecruisers defeat a German squadron at Dogger Bank</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Forewarned by codebreakers, Admiral Beatty's battlecruisers intercepted a German raiding force in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a> and sank the armoured cruiser <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gebhard-leberecht-von-blucher">Blücher</a>. Signalling errors let the rest escape.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1965">1965 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">61 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sir Winston Churchill dies aged 90</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s wartime Prime Minister died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, seventy years to the day after his father. He received a state funeral, the first for a politician since Gladstone.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1984">1984 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">42 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Apple Macintosh goes on sale</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Apple's Macintosh brought the mouse and graphical interface to an affordable personal computer. Launched with a famous television advert, it shaped the design of computers for decades.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 24 January <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/galeazzo-maria-sforza"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/galeazzo-maria-sforza.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Galeazzo Maria Sforza</span><span class="tp">1444–1476</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-the-great"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-the-great.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Frederick the Great</span><span class="tp">1712–1786</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gustav-iii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gustav-iii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Gustav III</span><span class="tp">1746–1792</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jaan-poska"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jaan-poska.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jaan Poska</span><span class="tp">1866–1920</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 24 January <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/david-iv-of-georgia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/david-iv-of-georgia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">David IV of Georgia</span><span class="tp">1073–1125</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-iv-of-aragon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alfonso-iv-of-aragon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alfonso IV of Aragon</span><span class="tp">1299–1336</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-ii-archduke-of-austria"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ferdinand-ii-archduke-of-austria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ferdinand II, Archduke of Austria</span><span class="tp">1529–1595</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/george-rooke"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/george-rooke.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">George Rooke</span><span class="tp">1650–1709</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/winston-churchill"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/winston-churchill.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Winston Churchill</span><span class="tp">1874–1965</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
